WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.114
Hi! Today we'll subtract four-digit numbers in columns, and learn how to regroup when a digit is too small.

2
00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:17.250
Start from the ones. 2 take away 8 won't work, so we regroup 1 ten: 12 minus 8 is 4.

3
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.602
The 4 tens became 3 tens. 3 minus 1 is 2.

4
00:00:22.752 --> 00:00:33.882
Hundreds: 3 minus 7 won't work, so regroup: 13 minus 7 is 6. The thousands went from 5 to 4, and 4 minus 2 is 2.

5
00:00:34.032 --> 00:00:42.858
So 5342 minus 2718 is 2624.

6
00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:49.938
Now 6000 minus 2457. The ones, tens and hundreds are all 0.

7
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:57.906
We regroup all the way: 6000 is the same as 5 thousands, 9 hundreds, 9 tens and 10 ones.

8
00:00:58.056 --> 00:01:09.978
10 minus 7 is 3, 9 minus 5 is 4, 9 minus 4 is 5, and 5 minus 2 is 3. The answer is 3543.

9
00:01:10.128 --> 00:01:20.994
Check with addition: 3543 plus 2457 is 6000. Correct!

10
00:01:21.144 --> 00:01:31.674
Watch out! Some pupils do 8 minus 2 in the ones and 7 minus 3 in the hundreds, and get 3376. That's wrong!

11
00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:39.522
We always take the bottom digit away from the top digit. If the top digit is too small, regroup from the next place.

12
00:01:39.672 --> 00:01:44.538
When you finish, check with addition to see if you're right.

13
00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:56.442
Your turn! What is 4876 minus 2531? Pause and think.

14
00:01:56.592 --> 00:02:05.922
Every column works without regrouping. The answer is 2345. Did you get it right?

15
00:02:06.072 --> 00:02:17.826
Another one! What is 7205 minus 3468? Pause and think.

16
00:02:17.976 --> 00:02:36.978
Ones: 15 minus 8 is 7. Tens: 9 minus 6 is 3. Hundreds: 11 minus 4 is 7. Thousands: 6 minus 3 is 3. The answer is 3737. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:37.128 --> 00:02:51.882
Here's another! A pail has 2500 millilitres of water. 1365 millilitres are poured out. How much is left? Pause and think.

18
00:02:52.032 --> 00:03:05.370
How much is left means subtract: 2500 minus 1365 is 1135 millilitres. Did you get it right?

19
00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:18.954
Last one! How can we check that 6000 minus 2457 is 3543? Pause and think.

20
00:03:19.104 --> 00:03:34.026
Add the answer to the number we took away: 3543 plus 2457 is 6000, the number we started with. So it's right. Did you get it right?

21
00:03:34.176 --> 00:03:45.690
Remember: in column subtraction start from the ones, and regroup from the next place when the top digit is too small. With zeros, regroup all the way along. Check with addition.

22
00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.690
Today, make up a subtraction question to test someone at home!

